        <mxCell id="note_scale" value="&lt;b&gt;How a version scales&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each WorkerResourceTemplate (order-fulfillment-scaler, checkout-abandon-scaler) is rendered by the controller into one KEDA ScaledObject per running build, so a ramping and a current build scale independently. KEDA's temporal trigger asks the frontend for that build's backlog every 15 s and sets replicas to ceil(backlog / 5) between 1 and 3; the floor of 1 keeps a draining build serving its pinned workflows. A drained build is scaled down after 1 h and deleted immediately after (deleteDelay 0 s)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="890" width="1720" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_scope" value="&lt;b&gt;Out of this picture&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;checkout-abandon writes only its own checkout database and calls no service. Both workers and the server export telemetry: worker SDK metrics go OTLP to the collector and on to vmagent; the server's four ServiceMonitors are scraped by vmagent. Workflow IDs, retries and the saga steps are in docs/api/temporal.md." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="962" width="1720" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
